# Format: stem|<cap>|reason, stem|slow <cap>|reason (measured only when named) or stem|unmeasured|reason
ltra_1|0.35|measured on its .save vectors; platform-dependent like its XFAIL entry (arm64 0.075, x86_64 0.239)
ltra_2|1.8|a 326-node lumped ladder driven by 0.1 ns edges at TMAX = 0.1 ns: the far end v(3), which stays near zero, carries a 0.12 V blip of unresolved ladder modes (1.3 V with the trapezoidal rule; 0.012 V at trtol=0.3). Reference at TMAX/80; measured 1.21
ltra_3|0.4|measured on its top-level nodes (measured 0.213 on arm64; the x3.* diode string snaps off in under a picosecond and held the deck at 3.3 when every node counted)
ltra_1_gear|unmeasured|already runs at the refined step; gated against ngspice in the golden check
ltra_3_gear|unmeasured|already runs at the refined step; gated against ngspice in the golden check
tra_pulse|0.25|measured 0.18, close to the default cap
uic_getic|0.25|measured 0.17, close to the default cap
vbic_uic|0.4|measured 0.316 at TSTEP 0.5 ns: a UIC start sets only the junction voltages, the internal nodes (collCI, baseBI) start at 0 V, and that first-step transient does not shrink with TMAX (0.538 at TSTEP 0.25 ns, the same with q1 alone)
cpl_3line|unmeasured|the CPL history is kept in integer picoseconds (cplload.c): refining its TMAX of 200 ps, successive runs differ by 10.4, 1.23, 0.29, 0.52, 2.27 and 4.95 rulers (/1-/5, /5-/10, /10-/20, /20-/40, /40-/80, /80-/160) - they stop converging below ~5 ps steps, and ngspice-47 itself at TMAX/80 and /160 differs by the same 4.95 (Dune at /80 = ngspice at /80 within 3e-13 V); fidelity is gated by the golden check
